<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">National Democratic Front (North Yemen)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1976">1976</a>–<a href="/years/1990">1990</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The National Democratic Front was a coalition of leftist groups founded in North <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yemen">Yemen</a> in 1976 in opposition to the government in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanaa">Sana'a</a>. Backed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-yemen">South Yemen</a>, it waged an armed insurgency in the central highlands from 1978 to 1982 and played a part in the brief inter-Yemeni war of 1979. Its members joined the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yemeni-socialist-party">Yemeni Socialist Party</a> at unification in 1990.</p></div>
